      "writtenOn": "2021-01-11T23:10:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You mean double-check that we\u0027re a sink before doing this?\n\nThe mechanism to prevent that is that the HV path is always the sink path, so we couldn\u0027t trigger OCP on it unless the sink path is enabled.\n\nBut I think we would want to bypass this in the case of an FRS, since the currents can get kind of crazy during that. There is an FRS flag we could use, but its probably better to include a sink flag to avoid race conditions. Thanks for the suggestion, I\u0027ll add that in.",
      "parentUuid": "3f9471ed_59ba3dd9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 275,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 278,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "97f8a9e545302b0f6e83277ddb518a4ec047d565",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54a27989_d9133f32",
        "filename": "driver/ppc/syv682x.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 278,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-11T23:15:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I don\u0027t think we\u0027re going to be able to avoid the race condition I\u0027m thinking of (OCP between the adapter removal and the reception of the FRS signal). So we could just use the FRS flag. But including the sink flag is probably better style, so I\u0027ll still do that unless there are objections to adding more flags.",
      "parentUuid": "89052d42_2705c094",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 275,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 278,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "97f8a9e545302b0f6e83277ddb518a4ec047d565",
